Chapter: DeskSpanTest
  cites Works chapter GopDesk

 Pins the span accessors the option-D allocator work reads: the extent of a
 mark-stack entry, the sum invariant over all of them, and the two questions
 that decide whether a dead entry's span may be allocated into.

 The fixture is a mark stack built by hand rather than by running the desk,
 because the whole point of these functions is to answer about stacks the
 desk cannot be made to produce on demand -- a buried dead entry with a live
 one above it, and a span holding the root.

Section: Fixture

 Entry marks stand in for heap addresses. They only have to be increasing,
 which is what `desk-marks-push` guarantees, so small round numbers make the
 arithmetic checkable by eye.

 The stack this builds, bottom to top: Files live at 1000, Editor live at
 3000, Browser DEAD at 7000, with the caller's frontier at 9000. Spans are
 therefore 2000, 4000 and 2000, summing to 8000, which is 9000 - 1000 and not
 9000 - base: the desk's own blocks sit below entry 0 and belong to no span.

  ds-top : Integer = 9000

  ds-build : Integer -> Integer
  ds-build (ms) =
    let a = desk-marks-push ms desk-focus-files 1000
    in let b = desk-marks-push ms desk-focus-edit 3000
    in let c = desk-marks-push ms desk-focus-bro 7000
    in desk-marks-depth ms

Section: Main

  opening : [Console] Nothing =
    let ms = alloc-zeroed 128 64
    in let d = ds-build ms
    in let kill = desk-marks-kill ms desk-focus-bro
    in act
    print-line-uni ("depth: " & show d)
    print-line-uni ("extent: " & show (desk-marks-extent ms 0 ds-top) & " " & show (desk-marks-extent ms 1 ds-top) & " " & show (desk-marks-extent ms 2 ds-top))
    print-line-uni ("sum: " & show (desk-marks-extent-sum ms (d - 1) ds-top) & " " & show (ds-top - desk-marks-mark ms 0))
    print-line-uni ("oob: " & show (desk-marks-extent ms (0 - 1) ds-top) & " " & show (desk-marks-extent ms 3 ds-top))
    print-line-uni ("holds-root: " & dk-yn (desk-span-holds-root ms 0 ds-top 1500) & " " & dk-yn (desk-span-holds-root ms 0 ds-top 3000) & " " & dk-yn (desk-span-holds-root ms 2 ds-top 8000) & " " & dk-yn (desk-span-holds-root ms 2 ds-top 9000))
    print-line-uni ("no-root: " & dk-yn (desk-span-holds-root ms 0 ds-top 0))
    print-line-uni ("reusable: " & dk-yn (desk-span-reusable ms 0 ds-top 0) & " " & dk-yn (desk-span-reusable ms 1 ds-top 0) & " " & dk-yn (desk-span-reusable ms 2 ds-top 0))
    print-line-uni ("root-blocks: " & dk-yn (desk-span-reusable ms 2 ds-top 8000))
  end
